Windows only. Lets Shared_brainflow-cerelog 932b3944 build with current MSVC
(Visual Studio 2026, toolset 14.51). macOS and Linux never compile either change.

1. src/utils/inc/get_dll_dir.h includes <atlstr.h> for one CString used to find the
   DLL's own folder. The build defines neither UNICODE nor _MBCS, and current ATL refuses
   to compile as MBCS, so every file including the header fails. get_dll_path is
   rewritten with plain Win32 calls (GetModuleHandleExA + GetModuleFileNameA, cut at the
   last backslash); the result is the same folder with a trailing backslash. Inside
   #ifdef _WIN32.
2. third_party/DSPFilters (used by DataHandler) aliases `tr1 = std::tr1` for every MSVC.
   std::tr1 was removed from MSVC's library, so it now takes the `tr1 = std` branch the
   other compilers use, keeping std::tr1 only for MSVC before 2015 (_MSC_VER < 1900).

Apply from the repository root:  git apply msvc-compat.patch

diff --git a/src/utils/inc/get_dll_dir.h b/src/utils/inc/get_dll_dir.h
